            <div xml:id="d142">

                <pb facs="0202" n="191" xml:id="pg191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.428/2068: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-18T16:00:00+00:00">February 18, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 18—11:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. Foreign Office note received on the projected voyage of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thorland</hi> to the Pacific halibut fishing grounds
                    states: “It has now been learned from the owners of the vessel that this project
                    has been abandoned for the current year.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
